<title>BRAZIL: Brazil allows 2.0 bln real loan to social security.</title>
<headline>Brazil allows 2.0 bln real loan to social security.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Monetary Council (CMN) Thursday authorized a loan of up to 2.0 billion reais to the INSS federal social security agency to cover 13th salary payments at Christmas, a Finance Ministry official said.</p>
<p>Pedro Parente, the ministry's executive secretary, told reporters the INSS would have to repay the loan to federal bank Banco do Brasil by Dec 26.</p>
<p>He declined to say what interest rate would be charged.</p>
<p>--Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358</p>
